+### pi.appendUsage(attribution)
+
+Persist usage from a standalone extension model call without creating a message or adding to actor context pressure. Pi includes each entry once in footer, `/session`, RPC, and HTML export totals.
+
+```typescript
+pi.appendUsage({
+  usage: response.usage,
+  provider: response.provider,
+  model: response.model,
+  operation: "my-extension:classify",
+  passId: "pass-123", // Optional correlation
+});
+```
+
+`operation` must be namespaced as `<extension>:<operation>`. Append returned usage even when the extension later rejects the model output. A custom entry may embed the same usage for provenance; custom-entry data is not counted in Pi totals.
+
 ### pi.appendEntry(customType, data?)
 
 Persist extension data. Custom entries do NOT participate in LLM context. In interactive mode, they can also render inside the chat transcript when paired with `pi.registerEntryRenderer()`.
