 Use `customType` to identify your extension's entries on reload. Interactive mode can render custom entries via `pi.registerEntryRenderer(customType, renderer)`, but they still do not participate in LLM context.
 
+### ExtensionUsageEntry
+
+Standalone model usage attributed by an extension through `pi.appendUsage()`. It is included once in session totals but does NOT participate in LLM context or context pressure.
+
+```json
+{"type":"extension_usage","id":"i8j9k0l1","parentId":"h8i9j0k1","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:22:00.000Z","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","operation":"my-extension:classify","passId":"pass-123","usage":{...}}
+```
+
+Fields:
+- `usage`: Normal provider `Usage`
+- `provider` / `model`: Model that produced the usage
+- `operation`: Namespaced `<extension>:<operation>` kind
+- `passId`: Optional extension-defined pass correlation
+
 ### CustomMessageEntry
 
 Extension-injected messages that DO participate in LLM context.
